{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454347-please-help-me-flesh-out-a-houserule-i-m-considering","id":1454347,"title":"Please help me flesh out a houserule I'm considering.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-06T06:31:49-07:00","id":1454347,"title":"Please help me flesh out a houserule I'm considering.","content":"I don't like that there doesn't seem to be much innate difference between the clans beyond their discipline spread. So I'm considering giving each clan two skills that they can develop for half price, rounded up. Or maybe a flat -2xp cost per dot. I'll have to playtest it a bit.<br /> <br /> So far I've come up with:<br /> Brujah: Intimidation and Streetwise<br /> <br /> Gangrel: Brawl and Survival<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: Stealth and Investigation<br /> <br /> Toreador: Performance and Persuasion<br /> <br /> Tremere: Occult and Awareness<br /> <br /> Ventrue: Leadership and Politics<br /> <br /> Past that I'm kind of at a loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T10:14:58-07:00","id":1454357,"title":"","content":"...That doesn't seem metaphysically right, and you'd be rewarding players for building their characters with low dots in things so that they can take full advantage of the discount. If I make a Ventrue with 4 leadership, and who puts 1 into something he intends to get 4 in, he's worse off than another ventrue who took 1 leadership and put his 4 somewhere else useful.<br /> <br /> Perhaps some free backgrounds would suffice. Or every clan choses to make one of two skills a 3 at character creation. I recall you're a V5 player and really, character creation in V5 tries to be very rigid for balance reasons, so you got to be careful of upsetting that balance. (Of course predator types throw that rigidness out the window but... eh.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-08-2021, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T10:56:15-07:00","id":1454367,"title":"","content":"i'm fairly certain each clan has exclusive merits and flaws or loresheets in V5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T18:19:02-07:00","id":1454403,"title":"","content":"The Laws of the Night LARP version did something similar to this, but it was basically free Ability Traits or Backgrounds. It was easier there because of the flat XP cost, rather than cumulative. You might look at that for some inspiration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T05:44:38-07:00","id":1454443,"title":"","content":"I've house ruled two Blood Gifts and one Clan Curse for each Clan, using the base Weaknesses from V20 and the Banes from V5 as the basis. See Changeling for a model of how that works (there you get two Birthrights and one Frailty).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T06:04:22-07:00","id":1454576,"title":"","content":"My suggestion is to develop clan differences using the city/setting in which you are going to play. Not an &quot;always true&quot; rule but a situational set of advantages (and eventually disadvantages).<br /> <br /> E.g.: due to the fact that one of the Brujah faction in the city is well connected in the union, all the Brujah have a Contact rating +1 if its reasonable that the are using this peculiar connection (and this could shape differences between Brujah factions, one with the union one with the street thug and so on). Or due to the well established ruling of the Toreador prince, all the Toreador under his wings gain +1 to Resource, thanks to this indirect patron relationship. I'd put no more than 2 of this clan differences/faction, otherwise the players could miss the additional setting layer. It should be a way to enforce the theme of a faction, not to give only an advantage.<br /> <br /> So no hard-homeruling for clan blood but instead thanks to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26404,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","user":"Submariner93","date":". 07-09-2021, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","name":"Submariner93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T08:48:18-07:00","id":1454580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Submariner93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454347-please-help-me-flesh-out-a-houserule-i-m-considering?p=1454576#post1454576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestion is to develop clan differences using the city/setting in which you are going to play. Not an &quot;always true&quot; rule but a situational set of advantages (and eventually disadvantages).<br /> <br /> E.g.: due to the fact that one of the Brujah faction in the city is well connected in the union, all the Brujah have a Contact rating +1 if its reasonable that the are using this peculiar connection (and this could shape differences between Brujah factions, one with the union one with the street thug and so on). Or due to the well established ruling of the Toreador prince, all the Toreador under his wings gain +1 to Resource, thanks to this indirect patron relationship. I'd put no more than 2 of this clan differences/faction, otherwise the players could miss the additional setting layer. It should be a way to enforce the theme of a faction, not to give only an advantage.<br /> <br /> So no hard-homeruling for clan blood but instead thanks to the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like that at all.<br /> <br /> I think each of the clans should have some innate advantages beyond simply having access to their disciplines. It's part of the lore that, for example, Gangrel are greatly feared in combat, when their disciplines alone simply don't justify it. Each of the clans should have a little something more to justify why they are feared in their main role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T06:42:40-07:00","id":1454649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454347-please-help-me-flesh-out-a-houserule-i-m-considering?p=1454580#post1454580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't like that at all.<br /> <br /> I think each of the clans should have some innate advantages beyond simply having access to their disciplines. It's part of the lore that, for example, Gangrel are greatly feared in combat, when their disciplines alone simply don't justify it. Each of the clans should have a little something more to justify why they are feared in their main role.</div> </div> </div> </div>The key thing to remember and balance around, is that clans aren't classes. They're loose archetypes that synergize with nature and nurture, given how each clan also has preferences for what sort of mortal they embrace, and how they train fledglings.<br /> <br /> Gangrel aren't feared in combat because they can land a solid hit or take one. They're feared in combat because they're brutal survivalists who never fight fair, use any and every tool at their disposal to win, and their discipline spread is perfectly suited for survival and asymmetric fighting on a level few if any vampires can compete. &quot;Fairness&quot; and &quot;honor&quot; are for gathers, and even then it's on Gangrels' terms, as applied to other Gangrel and other Gangrel alone. Brujah may be fantastic at the smashy-smash, but they don't hold a candle to the arsenal a Gangrel can bring to bear when it comes to guerilla (or gorilla) warfare.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, if you think Arms of Ahriman is overpowered due to its implications on action economy, try a Gangrel with a pack of animal ghouls that have been taught Celerity. Sure, Arms of Ahriman can be replaced by reusing Obtenebration 2 if they go down in combat, but Arms of Ahriman can't scout, convey messages, spy, or be possessed allowing their master to be active in daytime or with minimal risk to themselves, can they.<br /> <br /> And likewise, off-archetype play can be incredibly fun and powerful, and any house rule needs to thread the needle of not disrupting potential for off-type play or discouraging players from exploration. Again, clans aren't classes, and embrace preference/natural synergy with discipline spread only goes so far. To go with the earlier example, one of the nastier character concepts I ever put in a player's hands -- when one of my players in TC couldn't decide what they wanted to play -- was a Toreador with ECD (Animalism). <i>They</i> didn't realize what I'd handed them, but a couple other players at the table, who were vet players as well and played with me long enough to know my predilection towards Animalism, Auspex, and Presence, immediately recognized the implications of the character and were completely taken aback I'd actively suggest it at the table.<br /> <br /> That player figured it out pretty damn fast as soon as they figured out they could move more or less freely in action scenes with Celerity, dread gazing at will and allowing their animal ghouls to pin down and tear opponents to shreds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T16:48:25-07:00","id":1454664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454347-please-help-me-flesh-out-a-houserule-i-m-considering?p=1454649#post1454649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Gangrel aren't feared in combat because they can land a solid hit or take one. They're feared in combat because they're brutal survivalists who never fight fair, use any and every tool at their disposal to win, and their discipline spread is perfectly suited for survival and asymmetric fighting on a level few if any vampires can compete.</div> </div> </div> </div>All vampires are &quot;brutal survivalists who never fight fair, use any and every tool at their disposal to win,&quot; As for asymmetric warfare, Gangrel have one of the weakest discipline spreads for that. Malkavians are better, since they control information and people, making them perfect guerilla fighters, who can ambush/snipe easily, can not themselves be easily sniped/ambushed, and can make humans help them. Even Brujah are better at asymmetric warfare, since they can jump/climb to excellent ambush locations, or jump/climb to spots where there is little security when infiltrating, and easily get humans to help them. Nosferatu are better, since they combine stealth, the ability to jump/climb to useful locations, and are highly organized.<br /> <br /> What the Gangrel discipline spread is actually good at is rural utility. That is to say, they don't need havens and many don't need humans for food. They have the discipline equivalent of a wilderness survival kit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T23:15:30-07:00","id":1454674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454347-please-help-me-flesh-out-a-houserule-i-m-considering?p=1454664#post1454664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What the Gangrel discipline spread is actually good at is rural utility. That is to say, they don't need havens and many don't need humans for food. They have the discipline equivalent of a wilderness survival kit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until one remembers pest animals live in high numbers in cities as well, and tend to go unnoticed most of the time. Particularly those with predilections towards infesting food supplies, and/or carry communicable diseases. The last eighteen months being the perfect example of what can happen when the wrong animals end up in the wrong place, at the wrong time, and associated with adulterated food supplies.<br /> <br /> Those same animal species being specifically identified in VtM sourcebooks as ideal animal spies, saboteurs, and messengers due to high population and intelligence. What you're missing, is smashy-smash and shooty-shoot are just the tip of the iceberg here, and aren't really even the important part of what I'm discussing. Information, logistics, sabotage, and subterfuge being vastly more important, and humans more often than not being considerably more overt and unreliable than others within the animal kingdom for a vampire with Animalism. Good luck to Malkavians not of the Dominate &quot;bloodline&quot; getting humans to do anything with a sense of stability or reliability.<br /> <br /> I mean, I can't be the only person on these forums who's had a PC kill a Prince in a chronicle, with rats outfitted with teeny-tiny bomb vests, can I?<br /> <br /> And I mean, Potence and Celerity are great for movement and relocation, sure. They're also hideously expensive in blood cost, incurring cost <i>per round</i> for little return on investment compared to, say, literally being able to fly or access any possible location that isn't hermetically sealed. Fat lot of good a Brujah will be once they've starved themselves to get in the very sorts of positions you proscribe, given their clan flaw.<br /> <br /> The only clan you've mentioned that comes close to the ability of Gangrel in any of these things, are the Nosferatu. Obfuscate has an effective range, doesn't work on camera sparing the effect of a single merit, and outside that fairly constrained set of circumstances that play to their strengths they're walking Masquerade breaches who stick out like a sore thumb even among their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T19:51:46-07:00","id":1454932,"title":"","content":"I give each Clan and Bloodline in my games an Edge, a few minor mechanical benefits. Like Nosferatu have the ability to once a scene replace a die pool with their Humanity, and Ventrue win all ties. So I think it's a great idea, since Clan Disciplines as a means to differentiate Clans aren't really as big a deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}